# Barat Pay customer storefront — copy to .env.local for local development.

# Public origin of the API as the BROWSER sees it. Leave unset: empty means
# "same origin", so the browser calls /api/... on the host serving the
# storefront. nginx routes that to the API in production and next.config.ts
# rewrites it in development. Pointing this at a different site breaks OTP login
# and checkout, because the customer session cookie is Secure/SameSite=Lax and
# the API's CORS allowlist names the production origins only.
#
# Note this is the same variable the API validates as its own public origin
# (payment callback URLs, CORS). Setting it in a shared .env to anything other
# than the host that also serves this app reintroduces the cross-origin problem.
# API_PUBLIC_URL=

# Absolute address server components use, and the dev rewrite target. In Docker
# set it to the internal service address so RSC traffic never leaves the private
# network. Defaults to http://localhost:4000.
# API_INTERNAL_URL=http://api:4000
